WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.892
Sand gets trapped, but dissolved
salt passes through with the water.

00:00:04.152 --> 00:00:05.300
I remember that trap.

00:00:06.059 --> 00:00:06.589
Correct.

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:10.094
Filtration separates an
insoluble solid from a liquid.

00:00:10.347 --> 00:00:12.181
Sand on the paper is the residue.

00:00:12.690 --> 00:00:14.847
Liquid passing through is the filtrate.

00:00:15.310 --> 00:00:17.688
That filtrate still
contains dissolved salt.

00:00:18.047 --> 00:00:20.066
Clear does not mean chemically pure.

00:00:20.873 --> 00:00:24.289
To recover salt, I remove
water by evaporation.

00:00:24.802 --> 00:00:27.755
To collect the water as
well, I need another step.

00:00:28.524 --> 00:00:31.609
We can evaporate some water to
concentrate a suitable solution,

00:00:31.954 --> 00:00:36.436
then let it cool so crystals form,
filter off the crystals, and dry them.

00:00:36.830 --> 00:00:41.168
This is crystallization, and it is
often preferable to fiercely heating

00:00:41.183 --> 00:00:43.128
everything until completely dry.

00:00:43.877 --> 00:00:45.942
The teacher controls heating and safety.

00:00:46.344 --> 00:00:49.328
We are not giving the kitchen
an unexpected chemistry lesson.

00:00:50.141 --> 00:00:50.933
Exactly.

00:00:51.248 --> 00:00:53.477
Simple distillation collects a solvent.

00:00:53.802 --> 00:00:57.461
Water evaporates or boils,
the vapor enters a condenser,

00:00:57.690 --> 00:00:59.544
cools, and becomes liquid again.

00:01:00.009 --> 00:01:01.968
The collected liquid is the distillate.

00:01:02.375 --> 00:01:05.357
Dissolved salt stays behind
in the original vessel.

00:01:06.048 --> 00:01:07.940
Evaporation can leave the solid.

00:01:08.447 --> 00:01:11.869
Distillation collects the liquid
because it includes condensation,

00:01:12.081 --> 00:01:13.806
not because the water disappears.

00:01:14.510 --> 00:01:17.756
Fractional distillation helps
separate mixtures of liquids

00:01:17.756 --> 00:01:19.327
with different boiling behavior.

00:01:20.130 --> 00:01:24.495
A fractionating column enables
repeated vaporization and condensation,

00:01:24.765 --> 00:01:28.205
enriching the more volatile component
in the vapor collected first.

00:01:28.949 --> 00:01:33.506
That is how different useful fractions
can be obtained from crude oil rather than

00:01:33.506 --> 00:01:36.034
making new fuel molecules by filtering it.

00:01:36.794 --> 00:01:37.390
Correct.

00:01:37.796 --> 00:01:41.311
Crude oil fractions are themselves
mixtures with boiling ranges.

00:01:41.789 --> 00:01:45.963
Distillation is a separation method,
not a promise of perfect purity

00:01:45.970 --> 00:01:47.732
for every possible liquid mixture.

00:01:48.129 --> 00:01:49.340
One last toolkit.

00:01:49.783 --> 00:01:52.504
How could we separate the
colored dyes in a black ink?

00:01:53.266 --> 00:01:54.198
Chromatography.

00:01:54.573 --> 00:01:57.886
Put a small spot on paper and
let a suitable solvent carry

00:01:57.886 --> 00:01:59.561
the dyes different distances.

00:02:00.285 --> 00:02:00.910
Yes.

00:02:01.347 --> 00:02:05.048
Use a pencil baseline above the
solvent level so the sample does

00:02:05.050 --> 00:02:06.891
not simply dissolve into the beaker.

00:02:07.263 --> 00:02:11.292
The dyes differ in how strongly they
interact with the solvent and the paper.

00:02:11.729 --> 00:02:14.130
Mark the solvent front
before it disappears.

00:02:14.912 --> 00:02:19.584
If one spot matches a reference dye at the
same height, have we proved its identity?

00:02:20.387 --> 00:02:24.385
It is supporting evidence under the
same conditions, not proof by itself.

00:02:24.722 --> 00:02:28.357
Different substances can overlap,
and one visible spot does not

00:02:28.368 --> 00:02:30.001
guarantee complete purity.

00:02:30.324 --> 00:02:33.489
Other methods or another solvent
can strengthen the conclusion.

00:02:34.262 --> 00:02:37.841
What if my two liquids do
not mix, like oil and water?

00:02:38.637 --> 00:02:42.217
A separating funnel lets the
denser lower layer drain first.

00:02:42.631 --> 00:02:46.130
Magnetic separation can remove
iron from sand because iron

00:02:46.132 --> 00:02:47.526
is attracted to a magnet.

00:02:47.961 --> 00:02:51.481
Not every metal is magnetic,
so test the relevant property.

00:02:52.210 --> 00:02:56.507
Final challenge: iron filings,
sand, and salt are mixed together.

00:02:57.036 --> 00:02:58.589
How do you recover them separately?

00:02:59.465 --> 00:02:59.703
Use

00:02:59.703 --> 00:03:00.870
a magnet for the iron.

00:03:01.363 --> 00:03:03.086
Add water to dissolve the salt.

00:03:03.497 --> 00:03:07.351
Filter out the sand, then recover
salt from the filtrate by suitable

00:03:07.351 --> 00:03:09.279
evaporation and crystallization.

00:03:09.867 --> 00:03:11.857
Each step uses a different property.

00:03:12.584 --> 00:03:15.248
Oxygen contains bonded pairs of atoms.

00:03:15.599 --> 00:03:17.051
Element or compound?

00:03:17.855 --> 00:03:18.519
Element.

00:03:19.191 --> 00:03:20.898
Every atom is oxygen.

00:03:21.413 --> 00:03:26.101
A compound needs different elements
chemically combined, not merely two atoms.

00:03:26.826 --> 00:03:30.579
Can ordinary filter paper turn
saltwater into pure water?

00:03:31.456 --> 00:03:31.743
No.

00:03:32.339 --> 00:03:34.205
Dissolved salt passes through.

00:03:34.541 --> 00:03:37.680
Distillation can collect water
from a suitable salt solution.

00:03:38.027 --> 00:03:41.755
I must choose the method from the
property, not just the apparatus I like.

00:03:42.517 --> 00:03:43.217
Excellent.

00:03:43.687 --> 00:03:48.083
Read the particles, respect the formula,
and match the method to the mixture.

00:03:48.443 --> 00:03:51.333
The mystery tray is solved
without disappearing atoms

00:03:51.348 --> 00:03:53.151
or a single chemical cocktail
